  "query_preview": "..\nAn impending trough extending from Invest 97W to the east will move\nwestward through the region, bringing gusty winds, increased shower \ncoverage, and thunderstorm potential over the weekend, potentially \npeaking on Sunday. As 97W moves into the Philippine Sea, a monsoon \npattern will trail behind, enveloping the Marianas possibly for the \nentirety of next week. Because the timing of this pattern is more \nthan three days out, shower coverage was kept at scattered, however, \nincreasing into the late week to convey the possibility of the \nmonsoon strengthening. Winds will become moderate starting tomorrow, \nwith stronger gusts near heavier showers on Sunday before.",
